>
  <p><strong>In GTA 6 you can tear an ATM out of a wall with a winch and break it open for the cash inside.</strong> We tried it live on 2026-11-24. Below are the steps exactly as the game prompts them, plus what went wrong for us, so your first pull goes better than ours did.</p>

  <h2>What you need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A car with a winch.</strong> One guide says it's sold at mod shops under Bodywork, Towing, for $1,595. On our stream the SUV we'd fitted hooked straight on. A different car we tried later wouldn't hook at all, so use the car you put the winch on.</li>
    <li><strong>Explosives (optional).</strong> They're the quick way to break the cassettes out once the ATM is loose.</li>
    <li><strong>A plan for the cops.</strong> "Crime reported" pops up the moment the ATM leaves the wall.</li>
    <li><strong>A fence.</strong> The cash comes out as marked bills.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step by step</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>"Reverse the vehicle into the ATM to hook onto it."</strong> Back up to the machine until the hook catches.</li>
    <li><strong>Drive off</strong> to pull it out of the wall, then unhook it.</li>
    <li><strong>"Break the cash cassettes out of the ATM by dragging it around or by using explosives."</strong> Our sticky bomb did the job and the cassettes came out.</li>
    <li><strong>"Break open the released cash cassettes to collect the marked bills."</strong> Do it fast, because the cops are already on the way.</li>
    <li><strong>Get away and fence the bills.</strong> Your partner can take the bag to the fence while you lose the cops.</li>
  </ol>

  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:12px;margin:20px 0">
    <figure style="margin:0"><img src="/img/gta-6/atm/atm-winch-hooked.webp" alt="An SUV backed up to a wall ATM at night in GTA 6 with the winch hooked on and an Unhook prompt" width="880" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px" /><figcaption><small>Hooked on: the Unhook prompt means you've got it.</small></figcaption></figure>
    <figure style="margin:0"><img src="/img/gta-6/atm/atm-cash-cassettes.webp" alt="A ripped-out ATM on the street in GTA 6 with four white cash cassettes showing" width="880" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px" /><figcaption><small>After the blast: the cash cassettes are out and ready to break open.</small></figcaption></figure>
